From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wintrust: read catalog attributes and member attributes, reference tags

CryptCATEnumerateCatAttr, CryptCATEnumerateAttr, CryptCATGetCatAttrInfo,
CryptCATGetAttrInfo and CryptCATGetMemberInfo were stubs returning
nothing. The name/value attributes come from the catalog's extensions and
from each entry, listed in the reverse of the file order like the members.
A member's reference tag is its subject identifier when that is a zero
terminated string (what makecat writes), the hash in hex otherwise.
Two todo_wine marks in dlls/wintrust/tests/crypt.c are removed.

Gate: test/wintrustcat-gate.sh (64 and 32 bit; a catalog built outside
Wine). Mutants SG_MUTANT_CAT_TAGHEX, _ATTRORDER and _ATTRVAL are caught.
---
--- a/dlls/wintrust/crypt.c
+++ b/dlls/wintrust/crypt.c
@@ -52,6 +52,11 @@ struct cryptcat
     GUID      subject;
     DWORD     attr_count;
     CRYPTCATATTRIBUTE *attr;
+    /* name/value attributes decoded from the catalog extensions and from each entry, built when first asked for */
+    CRYPTCATATTRIBUTE **cat_attrs;
+    DWORD     cat_attr_count;
+    CRYPTCATATTRIBUTE ***entry_attrs;
+    DWORD    *entry_attr_count;
 };
 
 struct catadmin
@@ -725,6 +730,147 @@ BOOL WINAPI CryptCATAdminResolveCatalogPath(HCATADMIN hcatadmin, WCHAR *catalog_
     return TRUE;
